. R. Klén, M. Vuorinen, X. Zhang: Quasihyperbolic metric and Möbius transformations. Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 142 (2014), no. 1, 311-322, (arXiv)\n  131. R. Klén, M. Vuorinen, X. Zhang: Inequalities for the generalized trigonometric and hyperbolic functions. J. Math. Anal. Appl. 409 (2014), no. 1, 521-529. (arXiv)\n  132. R. Klén: Local convexity properties of Apollonian and Seittenranta’s metric balls. Conform. Geom. Dyn. 17 (2013), 133-144, (arXiv)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPubl. Math. Debrecen (https://publi.math.unideb.hu/paper/2138/download/10_5486_PMD_2017_7386.pdf)\nciteturn5search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.6 years ago; By PARISA HARIRI (Turku), RIKU KLÉN (Turku), ... ** Some sharp inequalities between the triangular ratio metric and the Cassinian metric are proved in the unit ball.\nPubl. Math. Debrecen  \n90/3-4 (2017), 269–285  \nDOI: 10.5486/PMD.2017.7386  \n\n# Some remarks on the Cassinian metric\n\nBy PARISA HARIRI (Turku), RIKU KLÉN (Turku),  \nMATTI VUORINEN (Turku) and XIAOHUI ZHANG (Joensuu)\n\n**Abstract.** Some sharp inequalities between the triangular ratio metric and the Cassinian metric are proved in the unit ball.\n\n## 1. Introduction\n\nGeometric function theory makes use of metrics in many ways. In the distortion theory, which is a significant part of function theory, one seeks to estimate the distance between \\(f(z)\\) and \\(f(w)\\) for a given analytic function \\(f\\) of the unit disk \\(\\mathbb{B}^2\\), in terms of the distance between \\(z\\) and \\(w\\), and their position in \\(\\mathbb{B}^2\\) [B1], [KL]. Distances are often measured in terms of hyperbolic or, in the case of multidimensional theory, hyperbolic type metrics, see [GP], [HIMPS], [K]. Some examples of recurrent metrics are the quasihyperbolic, distance ratio, and Apollonian metrics, see [GP], [B2], [HIMPS]. In this paper, we shall study a metric recently introduced by Z. Ibragimov [I], the Cassinian metric, and relate it to some of these other metrics. For this purpose, we first recall the definitions of the hyperbolic metric of the unit ball \\(\\mathbb{B}^n\\) in \\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\), and the distance ratio metric of a proper open subset of \\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\).\n\n### 1.1. Hyperbolic metric.\n\nRecall the definition of the hyperbolic distance \\(\\rho_{\\mathbb{B}^n}(x,y)\\) between two points \\(x,y \\in \\mathbb{B}^n\\) [B1]:\n\n\\[\n\\tanh \\frac{\\rho_{\\mathbb{B}^n}(x,y)}{2}\n=\n\\frac{|x-y|}{\\sqrt{|x-y|^2 + (1-|x|^2)(1-|y|^2)}}.\n\\tag{1.1}\n\\]\n\nMathematics Subject Classification: 51M10, 30C65.  \nKey words and phrases: hyperbolic metric, triangular ratio metric, Cassinian metric, distance ratio metric.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIDR@IIT Indore: Geometric properties of the Cassinian metric (https://dspace.iiti.ac.in/handle/123456789/6667)\nciteturn5search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Title:   | Geometric properties of the Cassinian metric ... The paper also deals with discussion on local convexity properties of the Cassinian metric balls in proper subdomains of RN.\n\nPlease use this identifier to cite or link to this item: `https://dspace.iiti.ac.in/handle/123456789/6667`\n\nTitle:   | Geometric properties of the Cassinian metric\nAuthors:   | Sahoo, Swadesh Kumar\nIssue Date:   | 2017\nPublisher:   | Wiley-VCH Verlag\nCitation:   | Klén, R., Mohapatra, M. R., & Sahoo, S. K. (2017). Geometric properties of the cassinian metric. Mathematische Nachrichten, 290(10), 1531-1543. doi:10.1002/mana.201600117\nAbstract:   | In this paper we prove a sharp distortion property of the Cassinian metric under Möbius transformations of a punctured ball onto another punctured ball. The paper also deals with discussion on local convexity properties of the Cassinian metric balls in proper subdomains of RN. Inclusion properties of the Cassinian metric balls with other hyperbolic-type metric balls are also investigated. In particular, several conjectures are also stated in response to sharpness of the inclusion relations. © 2016 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim\nURI:   | https://doi.org/10.1002/mana.201600117\nhttps://dspace.iiti.ac.in/handle/123456789/6667\nISSN:   | 0025-584X\nType of Material:   | Journal Article\nAppears in Collections:  | Department of Mathematics--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeometric properties of the Cassinian metric (https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.01298)\nciteturn5academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.0 years ago; Title: Geometric properties of the Cassinian metric ... The paper also deals with discussion on local convexity properties of the Cassinian metric balls in some specific subdomains of $\\mathbb{R}^n$.\nTitle: Geometric properties of the Cassinian metric\nAuthors: Riku Klén, Manas Ranjan Mohapatra, Swadesh Kumar Sahoo\nDate: Wed Nov  4 11:40:13 2015\n\nIn this paper we prove a sharp distortion property of the Cassinian metric under M\\\"obius transformations of a punctured ball onto another punctured ball. The paper also deals with discussion on local convexity properties of the Cassinian metric balls in some specific subdomains of $\\mathbb{R}^n$. Inclusion properties of the Cassinian metric balls with other hyperbolic-type metric balls are also investigated. In particular, several conjectures are also stated in response to sharpness of the inclusion relations.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRankless | Riku Klén (https://www.rankless.org/authors/riku-klen)\nciteturn5search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; 3  | On Jordan Type Inequalities for Hyperbolic Functions Journal of Inequalities and Applications ·Riku Klén, Mikko T. ... 12  | Lipschitz conditions, triangular ratio metric, and quasiconformal maps Annales Academiae Scientiarum Fennicae Mathematica ·Jiaolong Chen, Parisa Hariri, Riku Klén, Матти Вуоринен  | 2015 